From 403661bc7be2c99da38afd6f19b8e82fc6e3b795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bing Ho <bingh0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 22:54:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(win): reuse current window + sweep panes closed on exit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two regressions in the 0.2.0 Windows Terminal launcher vs. the intended
(tmux-matching) behavior:

1. `ccr` opened a SECOND window: `wt.exe new-tab` with no `-w` always spawns a
   new window. Add `-w 0` so it reuses the CURRENT Windows Terminal window.

2. On exit the sidecar lingered on "session ended": panes ran under `cmd /k`
   (kept open) and `ccr sidecar` looped forever. Switch both panes to `cmd /c`
   and add `ccr sidecar --exit-on-end`, which shows "session ended" briefly then
   exits — so both panes sweep closed on session end, mirroring the tmux
   launcher's `touch exited; sleep 2; kill-session`.

- sidecar.run() gains an injectable, flag-gated end-sweep (Linux/tmux and
  standalone `ccr sidecar` are unchanged — they never pass --exit-on-end).
- bin/ccr.js: parse `--exit-on-end`, thread it to sidecar.run().
- Tests: updated wt-args (-w 0, cmd /c, --exit-on-end) across unit + Gherkin
  steps; new run() end-sweep unit tests. 260 pass.

NEEDS WINDOWS VERIFICATION (untestable on Linux): that `wt -w 0` targets the
current window as intended, and the cmd /c sweep closes both panes cleanly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
